 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "When writing methods, I want you to get into the habit of always including docstrings.",
  "They provide a clear description of what the method does, and it's a best practice that will serve you well here at VERSA.",
  "Just ensure they're clear and concise.",
  "Just remember, clear communication is key, whether it's in our code or our day-to-day interactions.",
  "If you ever have any questions or concerns, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "That's what I'm here for!",
  "As you navigate your early career days, remember that continuous learning and improvement are key to your growth as a software engineer.",
  "First, set clear goals for yourself.",
  "Identify the aspects of Python you want to master and tailor your learning experience accordingly.",
  "Second, practice actively.",
  "Apply what you learn through coding exercises and small projects.",
  "Usually, we rotate between different venues and sometimes even do virtual happy hours to accommodate everyone's schedules and preferences.",
  "I want you to start using your company phone for work-related calls.",
  "It's important for client communication and maintaining a professional image.",
  "It's important to be consistent and clear in your code.",
  "Always include try statements in your methods to handle potential exceptions gracefully.",
  "This will help with error management and make your code more robust."
 ],
